      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "text": "Voice (CosyVoice) \u2014 two modes, one toggle (the 'switch' on the Mode select node).\n\n* switch = FALSE -> GENERATE: type text in 'Mode A' and upload a SHORT voice clip (3-30s) to 'Example voice (target timbre)' \u2014 CosyVoice clones it. A reference clip is REQUIRED.\n* switch = TRUE -> RE-VOICE: upload your speech (any length) to 'Source speech'. It is auto-split into <=25s chunks, re-voiced, and stitched back, so length is unlimited. The 'Example voice' target clip must stay SHORT (<=30s).\n\nFirst run downloads the CosyVoice model (~GB) \u2014 give it a few minutes.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Predefined example \u2014 it resets to the original every GPU start; edits here are lost. Save under a NEW name (Save As) to keep your own copy; custom workflows persist between sessions."
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Voice (CosyVoice) \u2014 two modes, one toggle (the 'switch' on the Mode select node).\n\n* switch = FALSE -> GENERATE: type text in 'Mode A' and upload a SHORT voice clip (3-30s) to 'Example voice (target timbre)' \u2014 CosyVoice clones it. A reference clip is REQUIRED.\n* switch = TRUE -> RE-VOICE: upload your speech (any length) to 'Source speech'. It is auto-split into <=25s chunks, re-voiced, and stitched back, so length is unlimited. The 'Example voice' target clip must stay SHORT (<=30s).\n\nFirst run downloads the CosyVoice model (~GB) \u2014 give it a few minutes.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Predefined example \u2014 it resets to the original every GPU start; edits here are lost. Save under a NEW name (Save As) to keep your own copy; custom workflows persist between sessions."
      ],
      "color": "#333",
      "bgcolor": "#444"
    },
